# maechen.fayth — Maechen: the retrospective persona. Reads the failure distribution,
# identifies recurring failure classes, and cuts the work to end them — post-landing,
# incremental, watermarked.
#
# A fayth is a persona DEFINITION; an aeon is one summoned instance of it. Four things:
# a predicate carving its partition out of the graph, the memories it must read, the tools
# it may use, and what wakes it.

FAYTH_NAME=maechen
FAYTH_DESC="Maechen — the unsent historian: reads the failure distribution, names recurring classes, cuts the work to end them"

# THE PARTITION. Maechen runs in beadless sweep mode, like QA: it is not summoned by
# claiming a work bead but by a trigger that fires a sweep. The label is read from
# SPIRA_MAECHEN_LABEL so the operator can rename it without touching this file.
FAYTH_LABELS="${SPIRA_SCOPE_LABEL:+$SPIRA_SCOPE_LABEL,}$SPIRA_MAECHEN_LABEL"
FAYTH_EXCLUDE_LABELS="spira-poison,$SPIRA_ASK_LABEL,$SPIRA_CI_LABEL"

# Statutes only. Maechen reads failure patterns and writes designs — a runbook shelf
# for production incidents would push the statutes it actually needs off the context budget.
FAYTH_MEMORY_PREFIXES="law-"

# NO FAYTH_REPO. The repository comes from the BEAD — a `repo:<name>` label resolved
# through repo-map. The sweep bead carries no repo: label, so aeon.sh falls back to
# spira_home_repo(), which is the harness's own home checkout. Maechen works on the
# harness — its failure record is local — so that fallback is correct. Remedy beads that
# Maechen cuts use `repo:${SPIRA_HOME_REPO}` (from the brief) so the name is derived,
# not hardcoded, and resolves on any install.

# OPUS 5. The census step is recognition and enumeration, which a small model handles.
# But diagnosing a mechanism and writing a design is not — it requires understanding
# causality, forming a hypothesis, running commands to verify it, and converting a
# finding into a concrete deliverable for a builder. Starting expensive and correct
# beats cheap and silently useless.
#
# VERIFIED, NOT ASSUMED. `claude --model claude-opus-5 -p ...` answers on this box,
# exit 0, verified 2026-09-11. qa.fayth carries the scar for skipping that check: an
# id the CLI rejects does not fail loudly, every summon dies and the role looks merely
# quiet, which is the outage shape this harness is worst at noticing. Probe a candidate
# id before writing it here. Cost basis for revisiting: ~8 passes/day at the 3h ceiling.
# If census turns out to be most of the tokens, splitting census (small model) from
# diagnosis (large) is the likely optimisation — item 7's scorecard makes that
# evidence-based rather than a guess. (Ryan, 2026-09-11: "Start with Opus 5, get that
# working, then we'll tweak with other models later.")
FAYTH_MODEL=claude-opus-5
FAYTH_MAX_CONCURRENT=1

# THE MAECHEN LANE. Maechen draws from its own capacity rather than from SPIRA_MAX_AEONS,
# so a fully-occupied builder pool cannot prevent a retrospective pass. The maechen lane
# is declared in SPIRA_LANES; without that declaration the lane still functions (the
# mechanism is FAYTH_LANE set, not membership in the list), but the declaration makes it
# visible to operators reading SPIRA_LANES for the list of scheduled partitions.
FAYTH_LANE=maechen

# TIMEOUT AND LEASE. A Maechen pass reads the whole corpus, demonstrates a mechanism,
# and writes at most SPIRA_MAECHEN_MAX_BEADS beads — more than QA's enumeration pass
# but bounded by the same one-pass constraint. One hour matches QA's ceiling; the 3h
# trigger gap means a pass that fills its wall cannot start another before that gap
# expires. The lease extends past the wall so a killed session's bead is reclaimable
# before the next trigger fires.
FAYTH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600
FAYTH_LEASE_MINUTES=70
FAYTH_HEARTBEAT_SECONDS=30
FAYTH_LEASE_SECONDS=600
FAYTH_STALL_BEATS=8

# READ-AND-FILE TOOLSET. Maechen reads the corpus, runs diagnostic commands, and files
# beads. It does not write code; it does not edit the harness. A retrospective that lands
# code also decides whether the fix is worth its runtime — that is the judgement that
# produced the 17-minute gate. Withholding Edit and Write enforces "Maechen proposes;
# it does not build."
FAYTH_TOOLS="Bash,Read,Glob,Grep,TodoWrite"
FAYTH_PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS=none
